⭐ 2. Core Equation

Let:

(\rho_b(\mathbf{x})) = predicted baryon density

(\rho_{\text{obs}}(\mathbf{x})) = observed baryon density

(M(\mathbf{x})) = observational sensitivity mask

Then:

[ \rho_{\text{miss}}(\mathbf{x}) = \rho_b(\mathbf{x}) - \rho_{\text{obs}}(\mathbf{x}) ]

Visible portion:

[ \rho_{\text{miss, vis}}(\mathbf{x}) = M(\mathbf{x}),\rho_{\text{miss}}(\mathbf{x}) ]

Reconciled inventory:

[ B_{\text{rec}} = B_{\text{obs}} + \int \rho_{\text{miss, vis}}(\mathbf{x}), d^3x ]

Residual discrepancy:

[ \Delta B = B_{\text{pred}} - B_{\text{rec}} ]

Finding:[ \Delta B \neq 0 ]

⭐ 3. Interpretation

A non‑zero residual (\Delta B) indicates:

the baryonic inventory model is incomplete

the observational framework cannot fully detect predicted matter

the ΛCDM baryon distribution rules require revision

This is a structural incompleteness, not an instrumental error.

